              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_ydqTfk": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Inside the settings menu (three vertical dots), you can find <strong>debug mode</strong>. There's a lot of confusing stuff in there!* </p><p>But if you're having trouble with one of your tools, or the network, you may find some answers.</p><p><em>*If you're an engineer, you'll probably love it. </em></p><p>If you're curious - signal strength is shown as a <strong>negative number </strong>(dBm). For reference: </p><p>-50 is fantastic</p><p>-80 is OK</p><p>-90 is marginal</p><p>And so on. </p>",
